# Tiny CPU loop: results

Randomly initialised byte-level transformers trained on CPU on the procedural bank (`data/generated/bank`, seed 1). These prove the pipeline, not model quality: the tiny teacher stands in for Gemma 4 31B and the students for Gemma 4 E2B. Test split, calibrated with per-primitive temperatures fitted on val. Generated by `scripts/run_tiny_loop.sh`; numbers are copied from each `eval/report.json`.

| model | core acc | ECE raw | ECE cal | Brier cal | log loss cal | choice acc | noul acc | score acc | box mean IoU | order agree | negation agree |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| tiny teacher, 2.1M params, log loss on code labels | 0.414 | 0.029 | 0.018 | 0.602 | 1.029 | 0.263 | 0.623 | 0.428 | 0.026 | 0.053 | 0.261 |
| tiny student, 1.0M, KL to tiny teacher + log loss | 0.416 | 0.032 | 0.025 | 0.594 | 1.018 | 0.263 | 0.638 | 0.407 | 0.092 | 0.037 | 0.320 |
| tiny student, 1.0M, log loss only (ablation) | 0.420 | 0.030 | 0.025 | 0.592 | 1.018 | 0.263 | 0.638 | 0.436 | 0.056 | 0.038 | 0.330 |

